-class CraftingItem;
+// KenshiCoop: CraftingItem is only ever forward-declared by KenshiLib, but the
+// 'crafting' member below is a std::deque<CraftingItem> BY VALUE, and VC10's
+// deque needs a complete element type (C2027).
+//
+// Defining an opaque stand-in is layout-safe: sizeof(std::deque<T>) does not
+// depend on T. KenshiLib's own offset comments confirm it - 'crafting' sits at
+// 0x498 and the next member at 0x4C8, i.e. exactly the 48 bytes a VC10 x64
+// deque occupies for any T. KenshiCoop never reads this container; it only
+// forms member-function pointers on CraftingBuilding.
+class CraftingItem { char _kc_opaque; };
 
